<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Cache Mountain</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:259-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.405262" lon="-121.861126"><ele>1458.1</ele><name>Ray Benson Sno-park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:ray-benson-sno-park (OSM way 205969667); confidence: high; pdf_page: 261; quote: The most obvious route to the top of Cache Mountain is from Ray Benson Sno-Park, by way of the South Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.381770" lon="-121.849040"><ele>1450.0</ele><name>South Loop / Brandenburg Loop junction</name><desc>source: OSM node shared by South Loop Ski Trail (way 822073235) and Brandenburg Loop Ski Trail (way 822073230); confidence: high; pdf_page: 261; quote: by way of the South Loop then on past Brandenburg Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.380290" lon="-121.837070"><ele>1434.6</ele><name>Brandenburg Loop east end, Roads 1028-600 / 1028-610</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Forest Roads 1028-600 and 1028-610, 0.2 mi south of the Brandenburg Loop Ski Trail's east end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 261; quote: by way of the South Loop then on past Brandenburg Butte and onto the Old Santiam Wagon Road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.378010" lon="-121.838440"><ele>1450.6</ele><name>Road 1028-500 (Old Santiam Wagon Road) at Road 1028-599</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Forest Roads 1028-500 and 1028-599; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 261; quote: onto the Old Santiam Wagon Road, a popular snowmobile route</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.371570" lon="-121.806920"><ele>1454.1</ele><name>Old Santiam Wagon Road at Little Cache Mountain (Roads 1028-500 / 1028-550)</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Forest Road 1028-500, Forest Road 1028-550 and the Santiam Wagon Road (way 5376774); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 261; quote: onto the Old Santiam Wagon Road, a popular snowmobile route that goes around the south side of Cache Mountain, called the Cross-District Trail by machine users</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.372030" lon="-121.789340"><ele>1549.1</ele><name>Road 1028-550 meets Road 2067-900, south of Cache Mountain</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Forest Roads 1028-550 and 2067-900; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 261; quote: A series of roads climbs the south side of the mountain with one going to the very summit</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.380500" lon="-121.780200"><ele>1699.9</ele><name>Cache Mountain summit (former lookout)</name><desc>source: OSM end of Forest Road 2067-900 (way 5348528), 22 m from the OSM Cache Mountain peak node 357307757; confidence: high; pdf_page: 261; book_elev_ft: 5579; quote: A series of roads climbs the south side of the mountain with one going to the very summit</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Cache Mountain</name><desc>1. Ray Benson Sno-park -&gt; South Loop / Brandenburg Loop junction: osm (high), 2.45 mi | 2. South Loop / Brandenburg Loop junction -&gt; Brandenburg Loop east end, Roads 1028-600 / 1028-610: osm (high), 0.93 mi | 3. Brandenburg Loop east end, Roads 1028-600 / 1028-610 -&gt; Road 1028-500 (Old Santiam Wagon Road) at Road 1028-599: straight (low), 0.17 mi | 4. Road 1028-500 (Old Santiam Wagon Road) at Road 1028-599 -&gt; Old Santiam Wagon Road at Little Cache Mountain (Roads 1028-500 / 1028-550): osm (medium), 1.66 mi | 5. Old Santiam Wagon Road at Little Cache Mountain (Roads 1028-500 / 1028-550) -&gt; Road 1028-550 meets Road 2067-900, south of Cache Mountain: osm (medium), 1.15 mi | 6. Road 1028-550 meets Road 2067-900, south of Cache Mountain -&gt; Cache Mountain summit (former lookout): osm (medium), 1.27 mi</desc>
